# Targets chezmoi should delete rather than merely stop managing. Removing a
# file from the source directory leaves the copy already on disk in place, which
# for a systemd unit means it keeps being loaded and started long after the
# source stopped describing it.
#
# hypr-session-save.service saved the session from ExecStop, outside the
# compositor: by the time it ran Hyprland was gone and there were no windows
# left to record, so it failed at every logout. The save happens inside
# Hyprland now (session.exit(), SUPER+SHIFT+M). The enablement symlink goes with
# it, or graphical-session.target keeps a dangling want.
.config/systemd/user/hypr-session-save.service
.config/systemd/user/graphical-session.target.wants/hypr-session-save.service
